There are a positive rational number $\delta$ and a rational character shift of arbitrarily small size for the ample rational linearized bundle $L+\delta J$ such that its stable locus $U$ is nonempty and equals its semistable locus. Every $x\in U$ satisfies $$\label{eq:weakweights}
w_L(x,\lambda)\ge0
\quad\text{for all integral one-parameter subgroups }\lambda.$$ The shift is used only to define $U$; the linearization on $L$ remains natural.
